---
title: Chicken Saagwala
servings: 4
time: 40 min
tags: chicken, curry, indian, main
cuisine: North Indian
course: main
---

If using frozen chicken strips, thaw them safely in the refrigerator and pat dry. Keep precooked strips aside to add near the end. Heat @neutral oil{2%tbsp} or @ghee{2%tbsp} in a #large saucepan{} over medium heat. Add @cumin seeds{1%tsp} and stir for 30 seconds, until fragrant.

Add @onion{1}(finely chopped) and cook until soft and lightly golden, ~{6-8%minutes}. Stir in @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) and @ginger{1%tbsp}(grated), and cook for ~{1%minute}.

Add @ground coriander{2%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @turmeric{1/2%tsp}, @chilli powder{1/4%tsp}, and @salt{1%tsp}. Stir briefly, then add the @tomato{1}(chopped). Cook until the tomato softens and the mixture becomes saucy, ~{5%minutes}.

Add the @spinach{300%g}(roughly chopped) and @water{100%ml}. Cover and cook until the spinach is wilted, ~{3%minutes}. Blend this spinach, tomato and onion masala with an #immersion blender{} until mostly smooth, then transfer the sauce to a bowl. Keep the pan off the heat while blending. The chicken, capsicum and frozen vegetables are cooked separately and do not go in the blender.

For raw chicken, return the pan to medium-high heat and cook the @chicken strips{450%g} in a single layer, in batches if needed, until cooked through, ~{5-7%minutes}. Transfer to a plate. For precooked chicken, skip this step.

Add the @frozen mixed vegetables{250%g} to the pan and cook until hot and tender, ~{5-7%minutes}. Add the @capsicum{1}(sliced) and cook for ~{2%minute}, keeping it slightly crisp.

Return the raw chicken to the pan, or add the precooked chicken now. Pour in the blended saag sauce and stir in @garam masala{1%tsp} and @lemon juice{1%tbsp}. Simmer gently until the sauce is hot and the chicken is piping hot, ~{3-4%minutes}. Taste and adjust the salt. Serve with @cooked rice{} or @naan{}.

> Swaps to consider: Add @?cream{2%tbsp} or @?plain yogurt{2%tbsp} at the end for a richer finish, @?fresh coriander{handful} as a garnish, or @?green chilli{1}(split) with the aromatics for more heat. Frozen chicken strips must be thawed before cooking; thawing time is not included.

> Source blend: ITV's Nisha Katona's Chicken Saag (https://www.itv.com/thismorning/articles/nisha-katonas-chicken-saag) informed the tomato, spinach, ginger-garlic and ground-spice base, and blending greens into the gravy. Simple Indian Recipes' Palak Chicken (https://simpleindianrecipes.com/palakchicken.aspx) contributed the onion-tomato masala and spinach puree technique, while Archana's Kitchen Saagwala Chicken (https://www.archanaskitchen.com/recipe/palak-chicken-curry-recipe-saag-wala-chicken) informed the cumin tempering and garam masala finish. The frozen mixed vegetables, capsicum and precooked chicken option adapt the dish to the owner's ingredients; their amounts and timings are estimates and untested.
